    "summary": "Explosive The Other One jam, tight first‑set classics and powerful second set",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a blistering The Other One extended jam alongside standout renditions of Bird Song, Cumberland Blues and Playin' In The Band. Phil Lesh provides a monumental bass solo while Keith Godchaux drives the band with hot keyboards. Soundboard recordings capture the high‑energy second set with crisp detail.",
    "review": "July 25, 1972 at Portland's Paramount Theater finds the Dead in top form, riding a tight first set of roots‑rock staples before launching into an electric second half. Early numbers like Bird Song and Cumberland Blues are played with crisp precision, setting up a soaring Playin' In The Band that showcases Keith’s driving piano work. The centerpiece is an explosive The Other One jam – a sprawling, Allman‑style excursion where Jerry’s lead guitar swings between fierce intensity and lyrical grace, even as he battles occasional tuning slips on Black Throated Wind. Phil’s bass solo during the jam feels like a seismic pulse, while Bill’s drums sit forward in the mix, giving the improvisation a solid, propulsive backbone. The set rounds out with a fiery Truckin', a soulful Wharf Rat and a jubilant double‑take of Not Fade Away that leaves the audience buzzing. Both soundboard sources are remarkably clear; Miller’s capture edges ahead with its overall balance and completeness, making it the definitive listening choice for this summer ’72 gem.",
